# {{group}} — group defaults

One default for every knob a group can decide for a repo's `.vegastack/dev.md` — the per-repo facts (`repo:`, `skill-scan:`, `board:`, `control-room:`) stay in the repo — so a repo that answers nothing else still gets a complete profile. A repo's own line beats every line here; this file beats `org.md`, except a line `org.md` marks `# locked`. Precedence and the read path: the vegafactory-setup skill's `references/control-room.md`.

## Knobs

merge: rebase               # rebase | squash | merge
branch: <type>/<slug>       # type: feat | fix | docs | chore | refactor
labels: waiting-on-operator planning queued in-progress ready-to-ship small medium large research risky epic   # the set itself; no knob renames them
tests: required             # required | logic-only | best-effort | none
changelog: changesets       # changesets | keep-a-changelog | pubspec+changelog | none
chronicle: on               # on | off
learning: normal-work       # normal-work | off
learning-adoption: scoped-reversible   # scoped-reversible | propose-only
operators: {{operators}}    # the logins who own issues in this group

## Harness policy

One line, `<stage> <agent> <model> <effort>` per stage, separated by `·`. `default` as the model pins nothing and takes the tool's own, which is the recommendation — a pinned id must be one the account can use. Confirm every stage; a placeholder blocks execution.

harness-policy: intake {{intake}} · plan {{plan}} · implement {{implement}} · review {{review}} · status {{status}} · chronicle {{chronicle}}

## Notes

Lines the workflow reads as prose, not knobs — a repo may say otherwise in its own dev.md.

- architect: {{architect}} — the architecture owner dev-architect speaks to.
- evidence-repo: {{org}}/{{evidence-repo}} — where UI screenshots and run evidence are pushed.
- ship-environments: preview auto · staging auto · production ask.
- design-system: {{design-system}} — the design layer a repo in this group consumes by default, or none.
- secrets: {{secret-names}} — NAMES only; the values live in the secret store.
- gh-floor: 2.97 — the minimum gh CLI version this group's automation assumes.
